From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Max Schaefer <max@excloo.com>
Date: Sat, 07 Nov 2026 19:19:11 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] 1058 redfin: keep direct scanout at the selected canvas size

Couple the existing opt-in sweetfb_native=1 geometry to scanout-slot
eligibility, automatic/direct swap eligibility and QSEED's source size.
Use the existing AppleCLCD owner's fLogicalW/H for surface eligibility,
not another copy of the native dimensions. sweet_fb_instance is published
before display registration; the earlier physical default surface is
created directly, not through the user-surface slot-eligibility path.

QSEED takes explicit source dimensions. Direct frames and occupied-slot
diagnostics pass the actual surface size. Fixed test patterns pass the
same 1125x2436 dimensions they were generated with. At native size retain
the existing scaler at unity, fence/latch/use-count gating, rowkeep1,
slot capacity and renderer behaviour. Default logical size stays 1125x2436.
No touch change is required: SweetHID already uses sweetfb_native.

This is a coupled, unactivated experiment: pair the boot argument with
mkadt.py --native-canvas, and observe actual 1080x2340 compositor surfaces
and 64-byte-aligned row pitch (normally 4352) before any performance test.
Never force or relax archived-row preservation to obtain direct scanout.
Native UI geometry and safe areas need device verification; there is no
Redfin rendering-correctness or performance result for this patch yet.

Provenance: current Redfin patched 1057 build tree, extending the local
0975/0976 slot/direct-scanout paths, 1046 automatic gate and existing
sweetfb_native framebuffer/HID selection. Existing copyright/licences
remain unchanged; no external scaler algorithm is imported.

